>This cannot be the intent as the comment on rnl(x) clearly states that the
>propability of x-1 should be decrease when luck increases.

Well, not quite; it states that rnl(x) should approach zero as luck
increases.  The lines I've marked 14-16 will indeed subtract a larger
amount from the result for higher values of luck; but line 13 slightly
reduces the chance of this subtraction occurring with high luck.  I believe
this will indeed reduce the expected value of rnl(x), as per the stated
intent, but it will *increase* the chance of getting *exactly* x-1.  I'm
too lazy to work out the exact probability distribution.

It seems to me that line 13 should use something like rn2(50 + Luck) or
rn2(25 + Luck) instead.

